===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|bretzel||dated}}
* {{alter|en|brezel||rare}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mreǵʰ-}}
From dialectal {{bor|en|de|Pretzel}}, a variant of standard {{m|de|Brezel}}, from {{der|en|goh|brēzitella}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*brāchiātellus}}, diminutive of {{der|en|la|brāchium}}, {{m|la|bracchium||arm}}; named for the appearance of folded arms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɛt.səl/|[ˈpʰɹɛʔt͡sɫ̩]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pretzel.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-pretzel.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛtsəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|culinary}} A toasted [[bread]] or [[cracker]] usually in the shape of a loose [[knot]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Anything that is knotted, [[twist]]ed, or [[tangle]]d.

